{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "metadata": {
  "note": "CTrail, the Connecticut Department of Transportation's commuter rail brand: Shore Line East (since 1990) and the Hartford Line (since 2018). Drawn as one company in one colour because CTDOT funded and ran both services throughout, whatever the contract operator (Amtrak for Shore Line East; TransitAmerica Services / Alternate Concepts for the Hartford Line). Shore Line East predates the CTrail brand, but it is the same state service under the same agency. Metro-North's New Haven Line, also CTDOT-funded but run as Metro-North, is in metro_north.geojson and is not repeated here.",
  "sources": [
   "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shore_Line_East",
   "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartford_Line"
  ],
  "not_yet_sourced": [
   "Every headway_min is estimated from a round-trip count, not counted from a timetable.",
   "The date the CTrail brand was applied to Shore Line East.",
   "How much CTrail Hartford Line service was cut during COVID (2020-21).",
   "Exact year the New London round trips went from two to six between 1996 and 2003."
  ]
 },
