    "geometry_quality": "Real traced geometry from OpenStreetMap rail (opstrace corridor Dijkstra over today's track, simplified to 8 m): 33.1 mi traced against 33.3 mi (New Haven MP 72.3 to Old Saybrook MP 105.6 from Grand Central) documented. No straight-line legs. Waypoints within 0.3 km of the drawn line. Draws today's alignment, which is also the alignment for every drawn year. Waypoints at Mill River and Cedar Hill were added to route round a break in the OSM graph east of Union Station; the result follows the Northeast Corridor throughout.",
    "segments": [
     {
      "start": 1990,
      "end": 1996,
      "headway_min": 120,
      "note": "Shore Line East began May 29 1990 between New Haven Union Station and Old Saybrook, a ConnDOT-funded service run under contract by Amtrak, started as temporary relief during I-95 reconstruction, per Wikipedia. Headway estimated.",
      "sources": [
       "Segment-level: this segment's own note names the source for its dates and service; the headway is an estimate, not counted from a timetable.",
       "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shore_Line_East"
